{"id":"8-cm-granatwerfer-34","slug":"8-cm-granatwerfer-34","name":"8 cm Granatwerfer 34","aliases":["8 cm sGrW 34","Granatwerfer 34","8cm schwerer Granatwerfer 34","8cm schwerer Granatwerfer 34/1"],"kind":"ordnance","category":"mortars","subcategory":"WWII German infantry mortar","description":"The 8 cm Granatwerfer 34 (8 cm GrW. 34) was the standard German infantry mortar throughout World War II. It was noted for its accuracy and rapid rate of fire.","history":"The weapon was of conventional design and broke down into three loads (smooth bore barrel, bipod, baseplate) for transport. Attached to the bipod were a traversing handwheel and a cross-leveling handwheel below the elevating mechanism. A panoramic sight was mounted on the traversing mechanism yoke for fine adjustments. A line on the tube could be used for rough laying.\nThe 8 cm GrW 34/1 was an adaptation for use in self-propelled mountings. A lightened version with a shorter barrel was put into production as the kurzer 8 cm Granatwerfer 42.\nThe mortar employed conventional 8 cm 3.5 kg shells (high explosive or smoke) with percussion fuzes. The range could be extended by fitting up to three additional powder charges between the shell tailfins.\nA total of 74,336,000 rounds of ammunition were produced for the Granatwerfer 34 from September 1939 to March 1945.","facts":[],"specifications":[{"group":"Cartridge & Action","items":[{"label":"Cartridge","value":"3.5 kg","numeric":3.5,"unit":"kg"},{"label":"Rate of Fire","value":"15-25 rpm"},{"label":"Muzzle Velocity","value":"174 m/s (571 ft/s)","numeric":174,"unit":"m/s"}]},{"group":"Dimensions","items":[{"label":"Weight","value":"62 kg (136.6 lbs)","numeric":62,"unit":"kg"},{"label":"Weight","value":"steel barrel"},{"label":"Weight","value":"57 kg (125.6 lbs)","numeric":57,"unit":"kg"},{"label":"Weight","value":"alloy barrel"},{"label":"Barrel Length","value":"1.14 m","numeric":1.14,"unit":"m"}]},{"group":"Performance","items":[{"label":"Effective Range","value"